tity lifecycle\n\nEntities have a well-defined lifecycle of **create**, **u=
pdate**, and\n**delete**. On each lifecycle update, Entity Manager emits th=
e state\nchange event back to Lattice:\n\n&lt;Steps&gt;\n  &lt;Step title=
=3D\&quot;Create\&quot;&gt;\n    When an app or integration publishes an en=
tity, Lattice emits a\n    state change event, setting the entity state to =
&lt;code&gt;CREATE&lt;/code&gt;.\n  &lt;/Step&gt;\n\n  &lt;Step title=3D\&q=
uot;Update\&quot;&gt;\n    When data in the entity changes, Lattice emits t=
he state change as an **update** event.\n    To optimize performance, Latti=
ce relies on changes to &lt;code&gt;provenance.source\\_update\\_time&lt;/c=
ode&gt;\n    to trigger an update. It does *not* compare the full proto def=
initions to set the state change.\n  &lt;/Step&gt;\n\n  &lt;Step title=3D\&=
quot;Delete\&quot;&gt;\n    An entity is deleted when its &lt;code&gt;expir=
y\\_time&lt;/code&gt; has lapsed, or an\n    update is sent with the &lt;co=
de&gt;is\\_live&lt;/code&gt; component set to &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt=
