<h2 id=3D"entity-lifecycle" class=3D"max-md:pr-4" data-state=3D"closed" sty=
le=3D"cursor: pointer;">Entity lifecycle</h2>
<p>Entities have a well-defined lifecycle of <strong class=3D"font-semibold=
">create</strong>, <strong class=3D"font-semibold">update</strong>, and
<strong class=3D"font-semibold">delete</strong>. On each lifecycle update, =
Entity Manager emits the state
change event back to Lattice:</p>
<!--$--><div class=3D"fern-steps"><!--$--><div class=3D"fern-step" id=3D"cr=
eate"><a data-astro-prefetch=3D"false" class=3D"fern-anchor" href=3D"https:=
//developer.anduril.com/guides/entities/overview#create" tabindex=3D"-1"><s=
pan class=3D"fern-anchor-icon"><span>1</span></span></a><h3>Create</h3><p>W=
hen an app or integration publishes an entity, Lattice emits a
state change event, setting the entity state to <code>CREATE</code>.</p></d=
iv><!--/$--><!--$--><div class=3D"fern-step" id=3D"update"><a data-astro-pr=
efetch=3D"false" class=3D"fern-anchor" href=3D"https://developer.anduril.co=
m/guides/entities/overview#update" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"fern-anch=
or-icon"><span>2</span></span></a><h3>Update</h3><p>When data in the entity=
 changes, Lattice emits the state change as an <strong class=3D"font-semibo=
ld">update</strong> event.
To optimize performance, Lattice relies on changes to <code>provenance.sour=
ce_update_time</code>
to trigger an update. It does <em>not</em> compare the full proto definitio=
ns to set the state change.</p></div><!--/$--><!--$--><div class=3D"fern-st=
ep" id=3D"delete"><a data-astro-prefetch=3D"false" class=3D"fern-anchor" hr=
ef=3D"https://developer.anduril.com/guides/entities/overview#delete" tabind=
ex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"fern-anchor-icon"><span>3</span></span></a><h3>Del=
ete</h3><p>An entity is deleted when its <code>expiry_time</code> has lapse=
d, or an
update is sent with the <code>is_live</code> component set to <code>false</=
code>.
Alternatively, you can use the <code>noExpiry</code> flag to create entitie=
s that
persist indefinitely. Use <code>noExpiry</code> only when the entity contai=
ns
information that should be available to other tasks or integrations beyond
its immediate operational context, such as long-living geographical entitie=
s.</p><div data-intent=3D"note" class=3D"fern-callout"><div class=3D"flex i=
tems-start space-x-4"><div class=3D"[&amp;_svg]:size-icon-md mt-0.5 w-4"><s=
pan class=3D"callout-icon"><svg data-prefix=3D"fas" data-icon=3D"arrows-rot=
